#
# ABox fixture for the estimand-framing competency question "which properties frame an
# estimand". One fully specified math:Estimand carrying each of the six ICH E9(R1)-style
# attributes that pin the target quantity before any data is seen: the population it targets
# (math:targetPopulation), the outcome it is defined on (math:targetOutcome), the contrast it
# measures (math:targetContrast), the intervention it conditions on
# (math:interventionCondition), the time horizon (math:targetTime), and the missing-data /
# intercurrent-event policy (math:missingDataPolicy). The reasoning-free query projects each
# predicate on the estimand. Unioned onto the merged ontology by gmeow:cqDataFile.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:estimand a math:Estimand ;
    math:targetPopulation ex:targetPop ;
    math:targetOutcome ex:outcome ;
    math:targetContrast ex:contrast ;
    math:interventionCondition ex:intervention ;
    math:targetTime ex:horizon ;
    math:missingDataPolicy ex:treatmentPolicy .
